# stack.branches: source of truth for this fork's PR branches and the combined main.
#
# Two concerns are kept separate on purpose:
#
#   * Each PR branch declares the base it rebases onto, 'base' (upstream, the
#     PR target) or another branch (a real dependency chain). This keeps every
#     branch's PR diff limited to its own work: independent fixes sit on 'base'
#     and never drag each other in.
#
#   * 'assemble' lists the order in which every branch's OWN commits are stacked
#     into the combined 'main' we run. main is a throwaway assembly of
#     cherry-picked copies, never a PR branch.
#
# Keywords:
#   base     <ref>               upstream ref; the PR target and default base.
#   into     <name>              the branch the assembly is written to.
#   branch   <name> onto <ref>   a PR branch; <ref> is 'base' or another branch.
#                                List a parent before any branch that sits on it.
#   assemble <name> ...          build order for the combined branch.
#
# Lines starting with # and blank lines are ignored.

base upstream/dev
into main

# -- compatibility blockers ---------------------------------------------------
# fix/fast-disk-kwarg removed 2026-09-28: upstream added fast_disk explicitly to
# both patchers (model_patcher.py:361 and :689) and forwards it, so the TypeError
# on every load_unet is gone. Our **kwargs version was only a robustness
# argument, and a weak one - FSDPModelPatcher overrides the load machinery, so
# silently forwarding a parameter it does not honour is worse than a loud
# TypeError. Do not refile.
# fix/xfuser-envs-get-device-name is superseded the same way: upstream now has
# get_device_name() at xfuser_compat.py:124. Out of the build; branch kept until
# it is confirmed unneeded on a render.
branch fix/xfuser-version-bound               onto base

# -- plain bugs, no knobs -----------------------------------------------------
branch fix/dead-actor-recovery                onto base
branch fix/ring-attention-lse-padding         onto base
branch fix/worker-nvrtc-library-path          onto base
branch fix/parallel-quant-shard-load          onto base
branch fix/forward-fast-disk-to-workers       onto base

# -- VRAM lifecycle (a real chain: cancel needs the progress plumbing) --------
# fix/sampler-progress adds _gather_with_progress, which the VRAM release path
# and then the cancel path both build on.
branch fix/sampler-progress                   onto base
branch fix/worker-vram-release-on-failure     onto fix/sampler-progress

# The text encoder reports progress and answers a cancel through the machinery
# fix/sampler-progress adds, so it chains onto it rather than onto base. File
# that one first if these ever go upstream.
branch feat/fsdp-text-encoder                 onto fix/sampler-progress
branch fix/sampler-cancel                     onto fix/worker-vram-release-on-failure
branch fix/offload-quantized-fsdp-shards      onto base
branch fix/free-host-vram-before-shard-load   onto base
branch fix/keep-host-models-when-gpus-pinned  onto base

# -- distributed VAE decode, and cancelling one ------------------------------
# The decode cancel checkpoint needs ray_worker_vae.py, which only exists here.
# That is why cancellation is two branches, not one.
branch feat/vae-temporal-chunk-decode         onto base
branch fix/decode-cancel                      onto feat/vae-temporal-chunk-decode
# The reserve fix edits ray_vae_decode_temporal_partial_impl, which the temporal
# decode adds, so it chains onto it for the same reason the cancel does.
branch fix/vae-decode-vram-reserve            onto feat/vae-temporal-chunk-decode
# feat/decode-pacer and feat/vae-decode-controls are out of the build, like
# tooling/fsdp-probes and tooling/crash-trace. They exist to investigate the
# host-heavy decode phase - the pacer spaces out when each card enters it, the
# controls narrow the fan-out and pin the VAE resident to bisect it. The reserve
# fix removes the phase, so both describe a problem the build no longer has, and
# their node inputs would be four widgets a workflow has no reason to set.

# -- features, all off by default --------------------------------------------
# fix/mlp-chunk owns the _mlp_branch extraction so the single pass and the per
# chunk path share one implementation. fp16 narrows that helper on its own
# terms, so the fp16-aware signature is a merge resolution here rather than a
# commit that belongs to neither branch.
branch fix/mlp-chunk                          onto base
# RESOLUTION NOTE: fix/mlp-chunk and feat/minimax-h3-fp16 each add
# `import os as _os` inside the MiniMax injector in usp.py, because each needs it
# on its own. Assembling both leaves the import twice - harmless, Python caches
# the module, but drop one when resolving the fp16 conflict. The two injection
# conditions union to `mlp_chunked or mlp_fp16 or <sidecar>`.
branch feat/minimax-h3-fp16                   onto base
branch feat/minimax-h3-fp16-node-inputs       onto feat/minimax-h3-fp16
branch feat/numa-aware-worker-placement       onto base
branch feat/lora-bypass-operand-placement     onto base
branch feat/rank-gpu-pinning                  onto base
branch fix/ck-patch-scope-nesting             onto base
branch fix/quant-loader-requires-grad        onto base
branch fix/ray-kill-without-model-load        onto base
branch fix/worker-pinned-memory-selectable    onto base
branch feat/worker-vram-tunables-in-workflow  onto base
branch feat/initializer-input-ux              onto feat/worker-vram-tunables-in-workflow

# tooling/crash-trace is NOT declared as a PR branch and is NOT in the build. Its
# markers sit in code owned by two different feature branches (encode_tokens from
# feat/fsdp-text-encoder, the decode path from feat/vae-temporal-chunk-decode), so it
# has no single base to rebase onto. It is built on top of an assembled main when a
# crash is being chased and rebuilt from scratch afterwards. An fsync per marker costs
# ~280 us and a shard load is ~1600 of them, so take it back out before quoting timing.

# tooling/fsdp-probes is deliberately NOT in the build: it is measurement
# scaffolding and any timing taken with it armed is unquotable. tooling/crash-trace
# is out for the same reason - it fsyncs a marker per phase, which is what made it
# useful against a host that resets without logging anything and useless for
# timing. trial/crash-trace holds the 2026-09-29 diagnostic state.
#
# tooling/stack IS in the build, and has to be: PHASE 2 checks out the base and
# cherry-picks, so unless the tooling is assembled too, the working tree loses
# restack.sh partway through and cannot be re-run after a conflict stop. It
# carries no code the node imports. It assembles FIRST so that after a conflict
# stop the working tree still has restack.sh to re-run - assembled last, the
# scripts only appear once the build already finished.
branch tooling/stack                          onto base

# Combined main = these branches' own commits, stacked in this order.
# ORDER MATTERS for node inputs: ComfyUI node inputs are POSITIONAL, and saved
# workflows store values by position. feat/rank-gpu-pinning inserts
# pin_ranks_to_gpus at index 4; feat/initializer-input-ux regroups the tail.
# Assembling rank-pinning BEFORE initializer-input-ux reproduces the input order
# the saved workflows in ComfyUI/user/default/workflows were built against.
# verify-restack.sh checks that order explicitly - do not reorder these two
# without re-running it.
assemble tooling/stack fix/xfuser-version-bound fix/dead-actor-recovery fix/ring-attention-lse-padding fix/worker-nvrtc-library-path fix/parallel-quant-shard-load fix/forward-fast-disk-to-workers fix/sampler-progress fix/worker-vram-release-on-failure fix/sampler-cancel fix/offload-quantized-fsdp-shards fix/free-host-vram-before-shard-load fix/keep-host-models-when-gpus-pinned feat/vae-temporal-chunk-decode fix/decode-cancel fix/vae-decode-vram-reserve fix/mlp-chunk feat/minimax-h3-fp16 feat/minimax-h3-fp16-node-inputs feat/numa-aware-worker-placement feat/lora-bypass-operand-placement feat/rank-gpu-pinning fix/ray-kill-without-model-load fix/worker-pinned-memory-selectable feat/worker-vram-tunables-in-workflow feat/initializer-input-ux fix/ck-patch-scope-nesting feat/fsdp-text-encoder fix/quant-loader-requires-grad
